-- source-break-continue-no-op: `break`/`continue` at the top level of a file run
-  with `.` do not reach a loop in the calling script (`builtin_source.c`
-  pushes a plain `E_ROOT` frame, which `eval_jump()` treats as a boundary).
-
-  **Repro:**
-  ```sh
-  echo break > b.sh; for i in 1 2 3; do . ./b.sh; echo $i; done   # prints 1 2 3; bash: nothing
-  ```
-
 - set-o-ignoreeof-nolog-vi-has-no-effect: `set -o ignoreeof`, `nolog` and `vi` are
   accepted and shown by `set -o`, but only store a bit: an interactive shell still
   exits at the first end-of-file, and there is no vi line editing.
